 "title": "gvylfs at price 6 (as gvyslzg6)",
 "question": "Does type sign x leverage, with leverage entering only through equity's fixed coupon (as asset composition does in BGN and KP14), give a fair gap above 0.02?",
 "notes": "WHY (2026-11-09). Section 3 asks the three models to be built the same way: a type-level loading b_f multiplies the firm's whole cash flow, and the within-firm state (asset composition in BGN and KP14, leverage in GS21) enters only through the model's own value / cash-flow structure, never in the exponent. PRECOMMITMENT STATUS: precommitted=false; ids filled from the Quest build log by the solve script before any seed runs.\n\nPREDICTION: the sign is hidden and leverage amplifies it, a product the linear model cannot hold; room and a gap. Whether the gap clears +0.02 depends on how much the coupon spreads equity's exposure; the endogenous-coupon version (gvy25s, gvy25sx2) had room 11-13% and no gap.",
